  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given an array AAA of size NNN, we must partition the array into 222 **disjoint** subsets S1S_1S1​ and S2S_2S2​ such that every element of AAA belongs to either S1S_1S1​ or S2S_2S2​. Further, we are given a parameter KKK and must ensure ∣S1∣≥K|S_1| \\ge K∣S1​∣≥K and ∣S2∣≥K|S_2| \\ge K∣S2​∣≥K, i.e. both S1S_1S1​ and S2S_2S2​ have size at least KKK.\n\nWe define score=min⁡(S1)+max⁡(S1)+min⁡(S2)+max⁡(S2)score = \\min(S_1) + \\max(S_1) + \\min(S_2) + \\max(S_2)score=min(S1​)+max(S1​)+min(S2​)+max(S2​), where min⁡(S1)\\min(S_1)min(S1​) is the minimum element present in S1S_1S1​, and the other terms are defined similarly.\n\nCompute the maximum scorescorescore in any valid partition.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line contains NNN and KKK - the size of the array and the parameter\nThe next line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,...,ANA_1, A_2, ..., A_NA1​,A2​,...,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the maximum scorescorescore in any valid partition.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤K1 \\le K1≤K and 2⋅K≤N2 \\cdot K \\le N2⋅K≤N",
      "1≤Ai≤1061 \\le A_i \\le 10^61≤Ai​≤106",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
